        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "eaa40bc1-0e1d-53f5-976b-29292fc4c945",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Daniel Mann, Daniel Chugerman, Todd Solondz, Derrick Tseng, Shirley Booth, Robert Ryan\n- Works: About Mrs. Leslie, Palindromes, Life During Wartime, Dark Horse\n- Roles: film director, television director, screenwriter, producer, co-producer\n\nFacts:\n- Daniel Mann, also known as Daniel Chugerman, was born on August 8, 1912, and he was an American film and television director.\n- About Mrs. Leslie is a 1954 American drama film directed by Daniel Mann and starring Shirley Booth and Robert Ryan.\n- Todd Solondz was born on October 15, 1959, and he is an American independent film screenwriter and director known for dark, thought-provoking, socially conscious satire.\n- Derrick Tseng was the producer of Todd Solondz's 2004 film Palindromes.\n- Derrick Tseng was the producer of Todd Solondz's 2009 film Life During Wartime.\n- Derrick Tseng was the co-producer of Todd Solondz's 2011 film Dark Horse.\n- Daniel Mann died on November 21, 1991.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
